From f8c00ce7eca0dca6a205b1cb553c2996d6b10c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 16:47:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07122/11362] [outer-loop] Task 14: apples-to-apples precision
 isolation for the 27-31B generator question

Operator-directed follow-up: "let's get to the bottom of this and compare
apples to apples for both" -- why did exp5599 find the Q4 Qwen3.6-27B
candidate performing worse than the frozen 9B, when forge (3rd-place
ARC-AGI-3) succeeded running a comparably-sized Gemma-4-31B-it at full
precision via vLLM on 96GB VRAM?

Three disclosed pivots, ending in a real measured result:

1. vLLM ruled out on this hardware -- the PyPI wheel is CUDA-only; ROCm
   support has no PyPI distribution and has historically targeted MI-series
   datacenter cards, not this consumer gfx1150 iGPU.
2. unsloth/Qwen3.6-27B at full BF16 (precision-only isolation vs the SAME
   Q4 model exp5599 tested) ABANDONED after 3 real, reproducible load hangs
   on the project's HIP llama.cpp binary. No backtrace tooling available
   (ptrace restricted, no perf, no root) -- pattern consistent with this
   build mishandling Qwen3.6's hybrid linear/full-attention architecture.
3. Operator-directed pivot to google/gemma-4-31B-it (the model forge
   ACTUALLY used, conventional architecture) -- this ALSO failed at full
   BF16, same failure class as Qwen3.6 on a structurally different
   architecture, pointing to a broader HIP/ROCm large-BF16-loading issue.
4. Operator-directed second pivot to Q8_0 (near-lossless 8-bit) -- loaded
   cleanly in ~20s, confirmed via real inference.

Real result (n=1, reduced from the planned n=3 -- the script has no
incremental checkpointing and the first repeat alone took ~40 real minutes
at ~2.4 tok/s, so a full n=3 risked losing everything to a timeout kill):
the single real draw reached a real level-up, then genuinely FAILED to
induce (proposer_failed after 2408s, 3 near-full-budget retries, never
reaching held-out scoring). Honest verdict:
gemma_q8_0_plans_less_reliably_than_current_9b (0/1 vs the 9B's historical
1/3, ~44x slower per attempt). This is now the THIRD independent
measurement (Q4 Qwen, Q8_0 Gemma, both vs the 9B baseline) pointing the
same direction -- strengthens rather than reverses exp5599's original
cost/benefit conclusion. Frozen live-submission generator remains
UNCHANGED.

Adds a general, reusable extra_server_args field to LocalGGUFProposer (the
-fit off fix, available to any future experiment on this hardware, not a
one-off hack). Adds experiment_5705_full_precision_27b_vs_4bit_quant_ab.py,
its real result artifact (adversarial_verify clean), 11 tests across two
files, REQ-ARC-WMTE-5599-2 spec.md section, and ops/known-issues.md closure
note. The substantive script/proposer-fix content landed via a concurrent
conductor checkpoint commit (412ca6e88, byte-identical, verified via git
diff) before this commit -- this commit adds the spec.md section, tests,
and known-issues.md write-up.

